{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791889510,"nonce":"LMc4DWNKkp1SEz70VnFiNsYKx3k=","message":"Read-only inventory and baseline reproduction while alignment milestone eaebad0/ecdb2f0 CI runs. Shared parser css/parser.rs::at_rule skips both constructs with warnings; Rule/Stylesheet contain media conditions only. Cascade matches rules against a single viewport MediaEnvironment. SDK Layout.compute restyles before native compute and already has bounded onLaidOut settling; Styles::set_environment marks the whole context dirty only when the viewport/scheme changes. Container dimensions and dependencies need native ownership rather than a JavaScript stylesheet rewrite.\n\nBaseline probe /private/tmp/blinc-conditional-baseline.mjs (results /private/tmp/blinc-conditional-baseline.json) gives identical runtime/compiled behavior: supported display:grid and invalid invented-mode supports branches are both skipped; the supported box remains100px instead of150px. At an800px viewport, a200px container has176px content width and a400px container376px after12px-per-side padding+border. Its two20px card children remain vertical after resize across a300px @container threshold. This separates ancestor content size from viewport and border-box size.\n\nOwnership check: clean shared ABI ecdb2f0; clean Ashui main9bd6471 and open trackers449ad47/8780d6b show general CSS gaps but no dedicated @supports/@container owner. Existing ABI worktrees have separate backgrounds, input style, object images, ordering, rowspan, calc, borders, generated content, fonts and gradients tasks; no conditional-query branch. Before source work, record the isolated shared-native prerequisite/ownership as required by fe65029.\n\nImplementation investigation: feature queries need property AND value validation, boolean not/and/or nesting, invalid/unknown false results and source-order behavior under nested @media/style rules; preserve compiled CSS compatibility and inactive rules/metadata rather than making compilation host-dependent. Existing is_layout_property/is_paint_property alone miss text/host declarations (including font properties and text-align) and do not validate the value. Parser capability must agree with applied behavior across SDKs.\n\nContainer size queries require nearest eligible authored/composed ancestor selection, container-type/name resets, content-box measurements and axis eligibility, then native dependency invalidation/re-cascade after layout. Containment must prevent descendants from influencing the queried size; fixed-width cards alone cannot prove that. Cover nested/named containers, threshold crossings in both directions, padding/border, query-unit font sizing, class/style changes, reparent/removal and settled idle behavior. Keep unsupported style/scroll queries and newer condition syntax explicit rather than silently treating them as viewport queries. Rust parser/codec/cascade/context tests plus runtime/compiled1x/2x Metal/Vulkan cards, HashLink compatibility and ordinary-renderer benchmarks form the next milestone gates.\n\nPrimary references checked: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-conditional-3/#supportsrule and https://drafts.csswg.org/css-conditional-5/#container-queries . No production source edits for ad2676b yet.","files":null}]}